  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FeSL (partially) implements the XACML 2.0 hierarchical resource profile [1]",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This enables resources to be specified as a \"uri\" [2] in policies [3], including specifying resources using regular expression matches [4].",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Only a subset of potential regex hierarchical URI specifications are used in the GenericPolicyFinderModule (actually -> PolicyManager -> DbXmlPolicyIndex) [5] which means that it is possible to create a policy using a resource URI with a regex which will never be located by the policy finder - thus the policy will never actually be used.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Example:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "To specify all members of a collection, it is necessary to specify the full URI path, including all parents, so for an example collection demo:collection which is itself a member of demo:topCollection, it is necessary to specify:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection/demo:collection/.* ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "to specify all members of demo:collection.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If demo:collection were to be moved into demo:otherTopCollection the policy would no longer work.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It should be possible to specify members of a collection using only the immediate parent, ie something like",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": ".",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "/demo:collection/.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "  (or something similar, regex probably needs tightening up a bit)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "However such a regex syntax would not be recognised by the policy finder, so the policy would never be used.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It is not possible to create a policy specifying \"all members of collection xyz\" without specifying all ancestors of collection xyz in the policy.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "NB: there will also be an impact on the hierarchical policy combining algorithms potentially if we change this behaviour",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "[1] ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/2.0/access_control-xacml-2.0-hier-profile-spec-os.pdf"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/2.0/access_control-xacml-2.0-hier-profile-spec-os.pdf",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "[2] in fact the \"uri\" used in FeSL isn't a defined Fedora URI, it's a simple path created by prepending all ancestors of the resource, separated by \"/\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "[3] using ResourceAttributeDesignator: urn:oasis:names:tc:xacml:1.0:resource:resource-id",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "[4] using ResourceMatch: urn:oasis:names:tc:xacml:2.0:function:anyURI-regexp-match",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "[5] an example of URIs that are generated for searching for policies are as follows for a request context specifying datastream DC in object demo:resource (with full collection membership as above).  Note that these would not catch all potential regex resource specifications that identify the resource:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection/demo:collection/demo:resource",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection/demo:collection/.*",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection/.*",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection/demo:collection/demo:resource/.*",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection/demo:collection/demo:resource/DC$",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection/demo:collection/demo:resource/DC",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "/demo:topCollection/demo:collection",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
