      "displayName": "A. Soroka",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A24c578cc-15e9-4649-9f68-5eace85735e0",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>This may be very much of an \"edge case\", but I can imagine situations in which our institution would want to record policy information in Fedora XACML that we don't expect the repository to enforce directly-- specifically, I'm thinking of \"gated discovery\", where we would want to record the information that some particular discoverable resource located outside the repository should or should not be discoverable by some actors. In that case, we might want to put an URI in the XACML that would never be resolved by Fedora in any important way.</p>\n",
     "created": "16/Feb/11 4:01 PM",
     "id": "11816",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10727/comment/11816",
     "updateAuthor": {
